\par }{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 Depending on the vagaries of La Poste you are likely to receive this Newsletter after our AGM on Thursday 9}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033 th}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 
 December. For those of you who cannot attend this meeting two items are worth recording here.  
\par Firstly David Blanchard has expressed his wish to stand down fro
m the post of Treasurer after a remarkable 20 year tenure in that office.  We owe him a great debt of gratitude for managing our funds with extreme professionalism.  He will be remembered not least for monitoring our smooth move from rue Boudreau to rue d
e
s Acacias last year, and making not only a capital gain on the disposal, but also investing at a lower price, so that we came out with a cash surplus, which we have in turn invested. As I will have announced at the AGM we do not yet have a candidate to su
cceed David, and so he has very kindly agreed to continue as acting Treasurer, including the task of coaching his successor whom we shall need to coopt.  I am sure that you wish us to mark David\rquote 
s retirement with a suitable event, and in the jargon of the Mess we propose to dine him out. We shall release details of this event shortly.
\par The second item which will have been discussed at the AGM is the motion which RBL London has required every branch in France to debate at their AGM, namely the formation of a D
istrict, akin to an RBL county organization in the UK.  This structure would have its own volunteer officers and committee, and would have certain federal responsibilities, principally in the financial and welfare domains, replacing certain of the functio
n
s currently carried out by paid executives in RBL London. At our AGM we shall be discussing the perceived advantages and disadvantages of such a structure from the point of view of a French branch like ours. We shall be required to vote in favour or again
st the motion, and if a majority of French branches vote in favour a district would be formed in 2011.
\par }{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 At our last Committee meeting we agreed to carry an advertisement in our Newsletter for first time, at least in recent memory. It concerns a private healt
h insurance scheme proposed by Charles Wilson, who will be known to many of us in the business community past and present. This form of complementary health care insurance will be of interest to some of our members, we believe.  Full details are to be fou
nd on Page3 below.  
\par Interestingly advertising as a potential source of donations to the Legion has apparently not been considered in the past.  We believe that we should encourage this form of support and if any member is able to introduce us to potential 
advertisers we should gladly examine such opportunities. Please write/e-mail me with the necessary introductions. 
\par We turn our minds now to the Branch events at Christmas.  We warmly thank Tony Bennett will be catering for us at both the Lunch on 15th December, and the Dinner on 17}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033 th}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 
 December. Our Social Secretary tells me there is a waiting list, so if you want to come and have not yet booked do not hesitate to call her on: 01.30.54.33.06 or 06.86.92.92.33.
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw30\brsp20 \nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 It now only remains for me to wish you and yours a Merry Christmas and a Happy, Peaceful New Year.
