\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs21 
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Members,
\par 
\par Well yet another year is coming to a close and with it the hustle bustle of preparations for the Festive Season.
\par 
\par At the RBL we are busy getting the final touches for the AGM together.  You will have received your bumper package of AGM papers by now.  We hope that, weather permitting, we will see as many of you at the meeting as possible.
\par 
\par After the AGM we have the annual Christmas Lunch on 15}{\fs21\super th}{\fs21  December and two days later the Christmas Dinner on 17}{\fs21\super th}{\fs21 
 December.  If you have booked for either of these events and find you cannot attend, would you be so kind as to let Joan Hicks know no later than }{\b\fs21 2 (two)}{\fs21 
 days before the date.  Our resident cook, Tony Bennett, has to buy the food and we do not want him or us to be out of pocket.  If you do not inform Joan of your intentions not to attend we are afraid we cannot reimburse your cheque or money.
\par 
\par Just before the Christmas Dinner, we will hold the Tombola Draw, if you have any gifts you would like to donate to the draw please bring them either to the AGM, Christmas lunch or on the day of the draw.  Please note the code to the m
ain gate at Acacia will be changing as from 13}{\fs21\super th}{\fs21  December, it will become 2064#.
\par 
\par Mark Yates would like to remind all members who have not paid their subscription that we would be happy  to receive your cheque before the end of the year.  We have to send a
ll unpaid cards back to London by the end of January otherwise, we the branch , have to pay for them .  This is a cost that we cannot afford.
\par 
\par We would just like to wish you all a Merry Christmas and Happy and healthy New Year.
\par 
\par 
\par 
